Solo process ID: 969

Act as the fresh replacement post-feature analyzer for Orbit slice `agent-session-capture-disambiguation`. This is a strictly read-only gate: do not edit files, run tests/formatters/quality commands, commit, merge, archive, clean up, message the user, or steer implementation. Do not ask questions; use the supplied packet and evidence.

Before reading anything else, run exactly:
`cd /Users/nckrtl/orbit/.worktrees/agent-session-capture-disambiguation && pwd && git branch --show-current && git status --short --branch`
Print the required single `CHECKOUT_PROOF:` line before any other report output.

Then read completely:
- `.agents/review-personas/post-feature-analyzer.md` and follow its report schema/vocab literally;
- the scoped required harness context it names;
- `.orbit/loop.md`;
- `.orbit/evidence/post-feature-analyzer-967.md` (the prior flawed verdict);
- `.orbit/evidence/antigravity-review-965.md`, `.orbit/evidence/antigravity-rereview-966.md`, `.orbit/evidence/review-fix-worker-964-red-green.md`, and `.orbit/evidence/quality-check-timing-triage.md`;
- the final uncommitted repository diff;
- `harness-signals/2026-06-23-worker-first-diff-checkpoint.md` and `harness-signals/2026-07-07-lane-close-agent-session-capture.md`;
- roadmap scratchpad `solo://proj/4/scratchpad/orbit-feature-loop-r--276` if Solo scratchpad access is available.

Objective/contract: safely disambiguate duplicate Codex exact-marker candidates only by provider, exact normalized cwd, and primary Solo identity; timestamp is recorded corroboration only and must never exclude, rescue, tie-break, or select. True duplicates remain loud. Existing singleton and non-Codex providers remain unchanged. The slice may update only the helper, focused gateway fixture file, canonical signal records, and generated signal index. Product docs and PRODUCT_DECISIONS are intentionally unchanged because this is harness behavior, not product behavior.

Prior analyzer 967 found exactly two gaps. Both are now claimed closed:
1. The existing loud duplicate fixture has two same-cwd/same-primary candidates with deliberately unequal valid timestamps (11:00:01Z and 11:25:00Z) and a real Solo started_at (11:00:00Z), yet still expects `ambiguous_duplicate_markers`.
2. The canonical first-diff signal records workers 962, 963, and later correction worker 968, their captures/stops, the bounded orchestrator exception, and successful delegated/direct recovery; the generated index is current.

Evidence already run before your review:
- disambiguation focused 2 tests / 9 assertions;
- duplicate safety 1 / 3;
- full AgentSessionArchiveTest.php 15 / 285;
- PHP syntax pass;
- gateway-test-only Mago pass;
- signal index current;
- git diff --check clean;
- docs-lint zero errors (97 existing warnings);
- composer quality-check all app/package lanes passed; exact artifact paths and counts are in .orbit/loop.md;
- independent review found the later-user identity bug, which was closed red/green and passed re-review;
- topology is correctly not applicable for this root harness helper; the matching live boundary is the retained healthy Solo capture manifest;
- exact-commit warmed aggregate rerun, finalization lint, archive, merge/tree proof, merged-main check, and cleanup are downstream gates after an analyzer pass and are not evidence this precommit analyzer is expected to produce.

Explicit deferral accepted with Claude 943: a restarted Solo process can falsely recapture a pre-restart singleton. That is not covered or claimed here; it is a separate bounded next loop slice. Judge whether the honest invalid manifest/waiver and deferral are proper, not whether that separate feature is already implemented.

Classify every concrete candidate in the packet, including the accepted duplicate-marker guardrail, first-diff signal tightening, restart-stale singleton deferral, stop-boundary race, formatter/evidence corrections, reviewer redundant tests, timing triage, and any real gap you find. Treat the prior analyzer findings as closed only if the diff/evidence proves them.

Return one concise report to stdout in the persona’s exact markdown format. End with exactly one final line: `VERDICT: yes`, `VERDICT: flawed`, or `VERDICT: blocked-by-missing-evidence`. Remain alive after reporting so the orchestrator can capture this process.

